<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Schedule widget, 4×2+. All colors, texts and glyphs are set at runtime by WidgetRenderer from
  the snapshot + WidgetPalette; the XML only fixes structure, spacing and type. Five columns are
  written out longhand because RemoteViews cannot loop. Direction is pinned in the XML, never
  inherited (D41: the APP language decides, and the launcher inflates under the SYSTEM locale):
  this file pins ltr, and the DERIVED Arabic variant (widget_schedule_arabic.xml) pins rtl, so
  each mirrors itself deterministically and Kotlin always fills children in natural order.
  Regenerate the variant with `bun scripts/derive-arabic-layouts.ts` after editing this file;
  never edit it by hand.
  The current column's ring is TWO FILLED layers (gold card behind, paper card inset 1.5dp on
  top), never a stroke-only shape: a tinted stroke drawable renders as a filled slab under the
  launcher's renderer — the exact owner-reported bug. forceDarkAllowed pins the runtime-tinted
  palette against OEM force-dark repainting. Column content is a CENTERED CLUSTER with fixed
  gaps — never weight-stretched apart: extra height becomes symmetric margin around the
  cluster, which reads as intentional space instead of emptiness (owner, 2026-08-25).
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
  xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
